  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNWOMEN GRANT MALAWI GIRLS CAN CODE TOO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Malawian Girls Can Code Too (MGCC2) initiative led by UN Women is designed to empower Malawian girls by building digital literacy and coding skills, thereby paving the way for them to pursue tech careers and generate income while accesing sexual reproductive health services and rights . This initiative also aims to leverage technology to enhance education, innovation, and gender equality awareness among youth, including those in remote regions (and young girls with disabilities), using inclusive strategies to bridge the digital divide.</narrative>
  </description>
